From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:56:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: report kernel 4.9 to the bpf loaders

netbpfload exits 3 on this kernel ("Android S & T require kernel 4.9.")
and the service's reboot_on_failure turns that into a
reboot,bpfloader-failed loop. The 4.4 kernel's bpf UAPI is the Android
backport that msm-4.9 also ships -- identical helper, program, map and
attach type lists (ours adds CGROUP_SOCK and the 4.14 jump encodings) --
so the version check is the only thing in the way.

ro.bpf.kver_override is read by both netbpfload/netd (Connectivity
KernelUtils.h) and the platform bpfloader, nothing else, so the override
is scoped to the code that gates on it. 4.9.0 keeps every bpf feature
decision at what this kernel actually implements; the remaining 4.9
accommodations come from the Connectivity and system/bpf patches.

---
 vendor_prop.mk | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vendor_prop.mk b/vendor_prop.mk
index 9ee5d7ae..bf2569ec 100644
--- a/vendor_prop.mk
+++ b/vendor_prop.mk
@@ -38,6 +38,13 @@ PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
     persist.vendor.audio.speaker.prot.enable=true \
     persist.vendor.audio.spkr.cal.duration=5
 
+# BPF
+# The msm8996 4.4 kernel carries the same Android eBPF backport as msm-4.9 (identical bpf UAPI:
+# CGROUP_SKB/CGROUP_SOCK, helpers through get_socket_uid), but netbpfload and netd gate on the
+# uname version and refuse anything below 4.9. Report 4.9 to the bpf code only.
+PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
+    ro.bpf.kver_override=4.9.0
+
 # Bluetooth
 PRODUCT_PROPERTY_OVERRIDES += \
     bluetooth.core.gap.le.privacy.enabled=false \
